      "text": "The solar eclipse of April 8, 2024, also known as the Great North American Eclipse, was a total solar eclipse visible across a band covering parts of North America, from Mexico to Canada and crossing the contiguous United States. A total solar eclipse occurs when the Moon's apparent diameter is larger than the Sun's, blocking all direct sunlight and allowing some of the Sun's corona and solar prominences to be seen. Totality occurred only in a limited path across Earth's surface, with the partial solar eclipse visible over a larger surrounding region."
