      "headline": "Diagnosed with Tuberculosis",
      "text": "Kafka was diagnosed with tuberculosis, a condition that would affect him for the rest of his life."
    },
    {
      "date": "1923",
      "headline": "Moved to Berlin",
      "text": "Kafka moved to Berlin to focus on his writing, living with Dora Diamant, a 25-year-old kindergarten teacher from an orthodox Jewish family."
    },
    {
      "date": "1924-06-03",
      "headline": "Death of Franz Kafka",
      "text": "Franz Kafka died on June 3, 1924, in Kierling, Austria, from complications of tuberculosis."
    }
  ]
}

