      "text": "Elon Musk led Tesla Motors' initial round of investment and became the chairman of the board of directors. He played a crucial role in the company's early development and strategy."
    },
    {
      "date": "2008-03",
      "headline": "Tesla Roadster Launch",
      "text": "Tesla released its first car, the Tesla Roadster, in March 2008. It was the first highway-legal all-electric car to use lithium-ion battery cells and had a range of over 200 miles per charge."
    },
    {
      "date": "2010-06-29",
      "headline": "Tesla's IPO",
      "text": "Tesla Motors went public on June 29, 2010, with an initial public offering (IPO) on the NASDAQ stock exchange, raising $226 million."
    },
    {
      "date": "2012-06",
      "headline": "Model S Launch",
      "text": "Tesla began deliveries of the Model S, a luxury all-electric sedan, in June 2012. The Model S received widespread acclaim for its performance and range."
    },
    {
      "date": "2015-09",
      "headline": "Model X Launch",
      "text": "Tesla launched the Model X, an all-electric SUV, in September 2015. The Model X was noted for its falcon-wing doors and advanced safety features."
    },
    {
      "date": "2016-04",
      "headline": "Model 3 Unveiled",
      "text": "Tesla unveiled the Model 3, a more affordable electric car aimed at the mass market, in April 2016. The Model 3 received over 325,000 reservations within a week of its announcement."
    },
    {
      "date": "2016-11",
      "headline": "Acquisition of SolarCity",
      "text": "Tesla completed its acquisition of SolarCity, a solar energy services company, in November 2016. This move was part of Tesla's strategy to create a vertically integrated sustainable energy company."
    },
    {
