      "text": "Lenin was arrested for his revolutionary activities and subsequently exiled to Siberia for three years."
    },
    {
      "date": "1903",
      "headline": "Bolshevik-Menshevik Split",
      "text": "Lenin played a key role in the split of the Russian Social Democratic Labour Party into the Bolsheviks and Mensheviks, leading the Bolshevik faction."
    },
    {
      "date": "1917-04",
      "headline": "Return to Russia",
      "text": "Lenin returned to Russia from exile in Switzerland following the February Revolution."
    },
    {
      "date": "1917-10-25",
      "headline": "October Revolution",
      "text": "Lenin led the Bolshevik Party in the October Revolution, overthrowing the Provisional Government and establishing Bolshevik control."
    },
    {
      "date": "1918-03-03",
      "headline": "Treaty of Brest-Litovsk",
      "text": "Lenin's government signed the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk, ending Russia's involvement in World War I."
    },
    {
      "date": "1918-1920",
      "headline": "Russian Civil War",
      "text": "Lenin's government fought and won the Russian Civil War against the White Army and other anti-Bolshevik forces."
    },
    {
      "date": "1921",
      "headline": "New Economic Policy",
      "text": "Lenin introduced the New Economic Policy (NEP), a temporary retreat from full socialism to revive the Russian economy."
    },
    {
      "date": "1922-12-30",
      "headline": "Formation of the Soviet Union",
      "text": "Lenin's leadership saw the formation of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics (USSR)."
    },
    {
      "date": "1922",
      "headline": "Health Decline",
      "text": "Lenin suffered a series of strokes, which began to severely impact his ability to govern."
    },
    {
