      "text": "Newton discovered the generalized binomial theorem, which would become a fundamental component of algebra."
    },
    {
      "date": "1665-1666",
      "headline": "Plague Years and Development of Calculus",
      "text": "During the Great Plague, Newton returned home and developed his theories on calculus, optics, and the law of gravitation."
    },
    {
      "date": "1668",
      "headline": "Construction of the First Reflecting Telescope",
      "text": "Newton built the first practical reflecting telescope, which used a mirror instead of lenses to avoid chromatic aberration."
    },
