      "text": "Alexander the Great conquers the Achaemenid Empire, leading to the decline of Zoroastrianism's influence as Greek culture spreads throughout the region."
    },
    {
      "date": "224",
      "headline": "Sassanian Empire and Zoroastrian Revival",
      "text": "The Sassanian Empire is established, and Zoroastrianism is revived as the state religion. The Avesta is compiled into a more organized form during this period."
    },
    {
      "date": "651",
      "headline": "Islamic Conquest of Persia",
      "text": "The Islamic conquest of Persia leads to the decline of Zoroastrianism as Islam becomes the dominant religion in the region. Many Zoroastrians migrate to India, where they become known as Parsis."
    },
    {
