      "date": "1917-06-04",
      "headline": "Establishment of the Order",
      "text": "The Most Excellent Order of the British Empire was established by King George V on 4 June 1917. It was created to fill gaps in the British honours system and to reward contributions to the arts and sciences, work with charitable and welfare organisations, and public service outside the civil service."
    },
    {
      "date": "1918",
      "headline": "First Appointments",
      "text": "The first appointments to the Order of the British Empire were made in 1918, recognizing the contributions of individuals during World War I. The order was initially intended to honor those who had served in non-combatant roles during the war."
    },
    {
      "date": "1922",
      "headline": "Introduction of the British Empire Medal",
      "text": "In 1922, the British Empire Medal (BEM) was introduced as a related award to the Order of the British Empire. Recipients of the BEM are affiliated with the order but are not members of it."
    },
    {
      "date": "1936",
      "headline": "Revisions to the Order",
      "text": "In 1936, revisions were made to the Order of the British Empire to include a broader range of services and contributions, reflecting the changing nature of British society and the empire."
    },
    {
      "date": "1940",
      "headline": "Expansion During World War II",
      "text": "During World War II, the Order of the British Empire was expanded to recognize the contributions of civilians and military personnel in various capacities, including those involved in the war effort at home and abroad."
    },
    {
      "date": "1957",
      "headline": "Introduction of the Chapel of the Order",
      "text": "The Chapel of the Order of the British Empire was dedicated in 1957 at St. Paul's Cathedral in London. It serves as a place of worship and reflection for members of the order."
    },
    {
      "date": "1993",
      "headline": "Reforms to the Honours System",
      "text": "In 1993, reforms were made to the British honours system, including the Order of the British Empire, to make it more inclusive and representative of modern British society. These changes aimed to ensure that honours were awarded based on merit and achievement."
    },
    {
      "date": "2012",
      "headline": "Reintroduction of the British Empire Medal",
      "text": "The British Empire Medal was reintroduced in 2012 as part of the Queen's Diamond Jubilee celebrations. This reintroduction aimed to recognize the contributions of individuals at the community level."
    }
  ]
}

